cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StudyGuard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "StudyGuard: a glass-box prompt coach for ChatGPT and Claude"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
authors:
  - family-names: Tate
    given-names: Eugenia
    affiliation: Duke University
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eugeniatate-duke/StudyGuard"
abstract: >-
  StudyGuard is a Chrome extension for ChatGPT and Claude. It scores, on the
  student's own device, how much of their own thinking a prompt shows, pauses
  prompts that only ask for the answer, and explains why with word-level
  attributions, counterfactual advice and a Prompt Breakdown Map. The
  repository includes a held-out evaluation, a red-team stress test, and a
  comparison of occlusion, LIME and SHAP explanations.
keywords:
  - explainable AI
  - responsible AI
  - education
  - Chrome extension
  - interpretability
